e policies for one storm. How SCWHUA, homeowners and flood claims interact, and where appraisal helps.</p><span class="go">Read the guide</span></span></a><a class="card rv" href="/appraisal-guides/appraisal-versus-lawsuit/"><span class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-2.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-2-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-2.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, (max-width:960px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="cb"><span class="meta">Oct 14, 2026 · 8 min</span><h2>Appraisal vs Lawsuit: Two Paths for a South Carolina Claim Dispute</h2><p>Appraisal settles price; a lawsuit can address much more. A plain comparison of the two paths, without legal advice.</p><span class="go">Read the guide</span></span></a><a class="card rv" href="/appraisal-guides/storm-damage-photo-checklist/"><span class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/hail.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hail-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hail.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, (max-width:960px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="cb"><span class="meta">Oct 23, 2026 · 7 min</span><h2>Storm Damage Photo Checklist for South Carolina Homeowners</h2><p>Photos are the evidence every adjuster, appraiser and umpire relies on. A room-by-room list of what to capture and how to keep it organized.</p><span class="go">Read the guide</span></span></a><a class="card rv" href="/appraisal-guides/how-umpires-decide-line-items/"><span class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/laptop-review.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/laptop-review-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/laptop-review.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, (max-width:960px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="cb"><span class="meta">Nov 5, 2026 · 8 min</span><h2>How an Appraisal Umpire Decides Disputed Line Items</h2><p>The umpire only rules on what the appraisers can’t settle. What that looks like item by item, and what makes a position persuasive.</p><span class="go">Read the guide</span></span></a></div></div></section>
